## 🔒 Contrôles de Sécurité Implémentés

### Kernel Hardening (NSA STIG)

```bash
# Paramètres sysctl de sécurité
net.ipv4.tcp_syncookies = 1
net.ipv4.conf.all.accept_redirects = 0
net.ipv6.conf.all.accept_redirects = 0
kernel.kptr_restrict = 2
kernel.dmesg_restrict = 1
kernel.unprivileged_bpf_disabled = 1
```

### Cryptographie Souveraine

```python
# Support cryptographique dual (NSA + Chine)
CRYPTO_PROVIDERS = {
    'nsa': {
        'algorithm': 'AES-256-GCM',
        'key_exchange': 'ECDH-P521',
        'signature': 'ECDSA-P521',
        'hash': 'SHA-384'
    },
    'china': {
        'algorithm': 'SM4-GCM',
        'key_exchange': 'SM2',
        'signature': 'SM2',
        'hash': 'SM3'
    }
}
```

### Audit & Conformité

```yaml
audit-rules:
  nsa-stig:
    - V-71849: "Audit must capture successful file system mounts"
    - V-72003: "Audit must capture successful modifications to user/group information"
    - V-73403: "Audit must capture successful modifications to cron jobs"
  
  mlps-level3:
    - "Audit des connexions utilisateur (90 jours minimum)"
    - "Audit des accès aux données sensibles"
    - "Journalisation immuable (WORM)"
```

